// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The shots. Each chapter is a list of beats; a beat starts at a caption
// (cap: 3 is the start of the fourth caption, 3.5 halfway through it) and
// changes only what it names:
//   panel: [recording, seconds in, rate, loop from, loop to]
//                                        the panel close-up from there; rate
//                                        0 holds the frame, and a loop replays
//                                        a stretch while the voice catches up
//   stage: [scene, seconds in] | "empty" what the comp viewer shows
//   sync:  [scene, run time, click time] start a scene so its command runs
//          as the panel recording clicks the button for it
//   focus: [x, y, zoom] | null           push in on a spot of the panel
//   wide:  true | false                  the viewer takes the whole frame
//   chip:  "Tab > Tool"            where the feature lives
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

